  "excluded": "Hosted triggers, schedulers, operational SQL, captured data and blanket grants are deliberately excluded. Local bootstrap supplies constraints, RLS and ownership separately. Cluster aggregate must use a scoped invoker view rather than an unscoped materialized-view grant.",
  "localDifferences": [
    "Local queue admits snapshot refresh and installation-owner achievement evaluation only",
    "Snapshot refresh uses a dedicated non-login non-bypass role",
    "Authenticated snapshot reads follow local guild membership",
    "No hosted schedulers, triggers, game credentials or captured state",
    "Selected core analytic definers use the non-login, non-bypass read owner. Catalogue tables allow authenticated reads only, with no public caller writes. Comprehensive player statistics remain service-only behind the canonical application authorization path.",
    "Local workspace recovery stores a digest only; code provisioning requires the current password and reset targets only the installation account.",
    "Empty file workspaces admit desktop_local_claim attestations without an upstream invitation. These represent local labels only, with automatic game sync disabled; they cannot establish upstream account ownership.",
    "A dedicated non-login non-bypass importer commits only the setup subject's guild and matching cluster, reads only raid conflict-key columns, and stores owner-scoped receipts. Caller roles cannot invoke the import primitive or inspect receipts.",
    "Meta-team memberships retain canonical rows and timestamps, scoped reads, own self declarations and same-guild leader overrides; local clients cannot write automated reconciler records.",
    "An own-key roster snapshot remains an explicit unverified local claim. A dedicated non-login non-bypass writer atomically commits its bounded cache, canonical mapped rows and local power; renderer roles cannot write cached payloads or invoke the primitive.",
    "Authenticated local planner-link writes use the canonical owner-only projection and a bounded HTTP(S) write validator; role, identity and credential columns stay read-only. Historical links and unrelated profile updates are retained while future link writes are checked.",
    "Canonical achievement inputs include guild-war attempts and computed raid awards. Owner-readable first-unlock rows are written by a strict durable local job; award calculation uses a non-login non-bypass reader scoped to the requesting installation. Guild-war input writes and module acquisition remain outside this selected closure.",
    "Canonical guild-team roster reads use a dedicated non-login non-bypass reader with membership-scoped RLS. Local members see only their own saved roster; no service-role or anonymous projection is granted. Desktop team comparison reads imported snapshots and does not invoke hosted roster backfill or live token overlays.",
    "Cached token reads use the signed-in local caller, the canonical membership guard and a non-login non-bypass reader. The explicit desktop token-state adapter preserves canonical math while using durable snapshot presence after disconnect and reporting cached provenance. It never acquires live data or synthesizes officer authority. Its peer-guild authorization explicitly aligns with current officer/leader roles (case-insensitive), while the canonical parent remains unchanged; admin is not an admitted membership role.",
    "Boss target assignments retain canonical constraints and current-member read plus officer/leader write policies. Authenticated callers have only target CRUD and read-only ops dependencies; anonymous access, blanket grants and unrelated orchestration writes are not selected.",
    "Historical comments are omitted from newly selected canonical raid-management functions. Source statement hashes retain the original bytes; executable SQL and mathematical expressions are unchanged.",
    "Saved season plans preserve canonical storage, constraints and current own-guild member/officer policies. Progression configuration is authenticated read-only. Native runtime roles receive no blanket plan/progression privileges.",
    "Exactly two public local saved-capability catalogue rows describe desktop preview availability only; they do not grant hosted entitlements or officer membership.",
    "An additional invoker-rights direct plan write trigger requires the signed creator on INSERT, immutable creator on UPDATE and a caller-visible baseline with the same guild, captured configuration season_id and numerical saved plan season. Canonical minimal JSON with both seasons absent remains compatible. Only the explicit native fixture and Auth owner roles bypass this guard for fixture enrollment and canonical ON DELETE SET NULL actions. Missing uid never grants runtime authority.",
    "The two saved-capability catalogue upserts change only local preview stage and route on conflict, preserving captured metadata and all unrelated catalogue entries.",
    "Selected saved-assignment intent uses atomic own-guild replacement and clear wrappers with exact lowercase active officer/leader authority, subject-bound bans and database-owned metadata; canonical parents are not client-executable. Direct RPC validates imported season and structural stage/roster inputs; captured lineup/as-of/model budgets are application admission, not storage authority. Global player mapping is never changed. A dedicated non-login non-bypass owner holds UPDATE(id) solely for FOR SHARE locks, with false mapping WITH CHECK. No broad authenticated ban access or stored forecast timestamp is admitted. A caller-bound paired read projects both selected-season intent arrays from one SQL statement snapshot, with one excess row exposed for decoder overflow refusal and no metadata identity fields."
  ],
